&lt;li&gt;Design and implement a unified multi‑entity consolidation and reporting model that can scale from today’s footprint to 2–3x the current number of entities and states, inclusive of inter-company transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition the organization from cash to accrual accounting where appropriate across entities and revenue streams (FFS, capitation, PMPM, grants, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize the chart of accounts, entity structure, and dimensionality (e.g., service line, market, payer, provider) to enable clear visibility into unit economics and contribution margins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accounting systems architecture across the group (ERP, subledgers, payroll, T&amp;amp;E, banking, and billing/RCM), ensuring clean data flow and a single source of truth for financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and reduce the monthly close timeline (currently ~20 days) through process, systems, and team improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the transition to a modern ERP system (e.g., Rillet), including implementation, migration, and integration with billing, capitation, and operational systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage core accounting functions, including AP, payroll, treasury, expense management, and tax, overseeing and developing a team of ~10 while remaining hands-on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with revenue cycle management (RCM) and billing teams to ensure accurate revenue recognition, cash reconciliation, and alignment between operational and financial reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with FP&amp;amp;A, operations, and market leaders to ensure financial reporting reflects business reality across entities and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with healthcare‑specific regulatory and reporting requirements (e.g., state health departments, payor contracts, risk‑bearing entity reporting) in partnership with Legal and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee tax and regulatory filings at the entity level (in coordination with external advisors), including multi‑state considerations and any risk‑bearing or provider‑group requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a geographically dispersed accounting team through a period of significant change, raising the bar on technical skills, ownership, and process discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a culture of documentation and continuous improvement, including developing SOPs, checklists, and playbooks for recurring processes (close, reconciliations, A/P, payroll, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of accounting experience, including experience as a Controller (or equivalent) in a healthcare services organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in a roll-up or multi-entity environment, ideally integrating acquired businesses into a centralized accounting function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with healthcare revenue models, including fee-for-service billing, capitation/PMPM, delegated or global risk arrangements, and other value-based care structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of improving close timelines, implementing systems, and upgrading accounting infrastructure in a high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing modern ERP systems and building scalable accounting processes from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical accounting foundation, with the ability to navigate complexity across entities, states, and revenue streams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive communicator who builds strong cross-functional relationships—understanding that high-quality accounting requires deep partnership with operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on and detail-oriented, but equally capable of stepping back to design systems that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity and building structure in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accounting systems architecture across the group (ERP, subledgers, payroll, T&amp;amp;E, banking, and billing/RCM), ensuring clean data flow and a single source of truth for financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize the chart of accounts, entity structure, and dimensionality (e.g., service line, market, payer, provider) to enable clear visibility into unit economics and contribution margins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with modern tools and data environments (e.g., cloud ERP, embedded analytics/BI, workflow tools) and partnering with engineering or data teams to improve data quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience designing or re‑designing chart of accounts and reporting structures for multi‑entity, multi‑state healthcare or services businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating healthcare regulatory and payor environments (e.g., delegated risk, MSOs, provider groups, or health plans), and understanding how operational nuances translate into revenue and accruals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to risk‑bearing entities or value‑based care arrangements is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
