&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Akido builds AI-powered doctors&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Akido is the first AI-native care provider, combining cutting-edge technology with a nationwide medical network to address America’s physician shortage and make exceptional healthcare universal. Its AI empowers doctors to deliver faster, more accurate, and more compassionate care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving 500K+ patients across California, Rhode Island, and New York, Akido offers primary and specialty care in 26 specialties—from serving&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fastcompany.com/91231274/how-one-la-doctor-is-using-ai-to-help-homeless-communities-get-medical-care&quot;&gt;unhoused communities&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;in Los Angeles to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-ai-doctor-will-see-new-york-ride-share-drivers-now-5ba53e6c?mod=Searchresults_pos1&amp;amp;page=1&quot;&gt;ride-share drivers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;in New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2015 (YC W15), Akido is expanding its risk-bearing care models and scaling&amp;nbsp;ScopeAI, its breakthrough clinical AI platform. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250515102298/en/Akido-Raises-%2460-Million-Series-B-to-Expand-Reach-of-ScopeAI-its-Breakthrough-Health-Artificial-Intelligence&quot;&gt;Read more about Akido’s $60M Series B&lt;/a&gt;. More info at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Akidolabs.com&quot;&gt;Akidolabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;1269&quot; data-end=&quot;1287&quot;&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1289&quot; data-end=&quot;1576&quot;&gt;Akido is hiring &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1305&quot; data-end=&quot;1327&quot;&gt;Housing Navigators&lt;/strong&gt; to support our Community Supports Housing programs in &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1382&quot; data-end=&quot;1420&quot;&gt;Los Angeles County and Kern County&lt;/strong&gt;. This role is central to helping members experiencing homelessness or housing instability successfully transition into housing and maintain stable tenancy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1578&quot; data-end=&quot;1823&quot;&gt;Housing Navigators work directly with members, landlords, care teams, and community partners to deliver &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1682&quot; data-end=&quot;1731&quot;&gt;Housing Transition Navigation Services (HTNS)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1733&quot; data-end=&quot;1753&quot;&gt;Housing Deposits&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1759&quot; data-end=&quot;1809&quot;&gt;Housing Tenancy and Sustaining Services (HTSS)&lt;/strong&gt; under CalAIM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1825&quot; data-end=&quot;2034&quot;&gt;This role blends &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1842&quot; data-end=&quot;1868&quot;&gt;field-based engagement&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1874&quot; data-end=&quot;1919&quot;&gt;structured documentation and coordination&lt;/strong&gt;, ideal for someone who understands housing systems, enjoys problem-solving, and is motivated by measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2036&quot; data-end=&quot;2039&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;2041&quot; data-end=&quot;2058&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2060&quot; data-end=&quot;2107&quot;&gt;Housing Transition Navigation (Pre-Tenancy)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2111&quot; data-end=&quot;2202&quot;&gt;Conduct housing assessments to identify member needs, preferences, barriers, and strengths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2205&quot; data-end=&quot;2292&quot;&gt;Complete and maintain Housing Plans in accordance with Community Supports requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2295&quot; data-end=&quot;2315&quot;&gt;Assist members with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2320&quot; data-end=&quot;2360&quot;&gt;Housing searches and unit identification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2365&quot; data-end=&quot;2396&quot;&gt;Completing housing applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2401&quot; data-end=&quot;2493&quot;&gt;Gathering required documentation (ID, SS card, income verification, disability verification)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2496&quot; data-end=&quot;2595&quot;&gt;Conduct or support VI-SPDAT completion when required and coordinate with Coordinated Entry Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2598&quot; data-end=&quot;2676&quot;&gt;Educate members on tenant rights, fair housing, and reasonable accommodations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2679&quot; data-end=&quot;2768&quot;&gt;Engage landlords and property managers to support housing placement and resolve barriers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2771&quot; data-end=&quot;2861&quot;&gt;Coordinate move-in logistics, including inspections, utility setup, and move-in readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2863&quot; data-end=&quot;2908&quot;&gt;Housing Deposits &amp;amp; Financial Coordination&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2912&quot; data-end=&quot;3031&quot;&gt;Identify and secure eligible Housing Deposit resources (security deposits, utilities, application fees, move-in costs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3034&quot; data-end=&quot;3137&quot;&gt;Prepare and submit Housing Deposit requests and supporting documentation for health plan authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3140&quot; data-end=&quot;3232&quot;&gt;Track approval status, timelines, and disbursement coordination with internal finance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3235&quot; data-end=&quot;3308&quot;&gt;Ensure deposits align with approved housing plans and program guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;3310&quot; data-end=&quot;3366&quot;&gt;Housing Tenancy &amp;amp; Sustaining Services (Post-Move-In)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3370&quot; data-end=&quot;3442&quot;&gt;Provide ongoing tenancy support to help members maintain stable housing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3445&quot; data-end=&quot;3520&quot;&gt;Support lease compliance, household management, and landlord communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3523&quot; data-end=&quot;3626&quot;&gt;Identify early warning signs of housing instability (late rent, lease violations, behavioral concerns).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3629&quot; data-end=&quot;3714&quot;&gt;Assist with conflict resolution, repayment plans, and eviction prevention strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3717&quot; data-end=&quot;3782&quot;&gt;Support annual recertifications and ongoing housing plan updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3785&quot; data-end=&quot;3884&quot;&gt;Link members to community resources (benefits, behavioral health, financial literacy, life skills).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;3886&quot; data-end=&quot;3925&quot;&gt;Documentation, Billing &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3929&quot; data-end=&quot;4012&quot;&gt;Maintain timely, accurate documentation in Akido’s EHR and case management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4015&quot; data-end=&quot;4101&quot;&gt;Ensure services align with authorization requirements and billable activity standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4104&quot; data-end=&quot;4180&quot;&gt;Track time spent and activities in compliance with Housing CS billing rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4183&quot; data-end=&quot;4254&quot;&gt;Coordinate closely with care managers, ECM teams, and operations staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4257&quot; data-end=&quot;4327&quot;&gt;Participate in case conferences, huddles, and supervision as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;4329&quot; data-end=&quot;4355&quot;&gt;Team &amp;amp; Program Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4359&quot; data-end=&quot;4458&quot;&gt;Serve as a key liaison between members, providers, landlords, health plans, and community partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4461&quot; data-end=&quot;4513&quot;&gt;Support outreach and engagement efforts when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4516&quot; data-end=&quot;4578&quot;&gt;Identify workflow gaps and contribute to process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4581&quot; data-end=&quot;4629&quot;&gt;Other duties as assigned based on program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;4631&quot; data-end=&quot;4634&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;4636&quot; data-end=&quot;4650&quot;&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4654&quot; data-end=&quot;4749&quot;&gt;3+ year experience in housing navigation, case management, social services, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4752&quot; data-end=&quot;4772&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4777&quot; data-end=&quot;4802&quot;&gt;Homeless services systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4807&quot; data-end=&quot;4837&quot;&gt;Coordinated Entry and VI-SPDAT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4842&quot; data-end=&quot;4885&quot;&gt;Housing First and harm reduction principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4890&quot; data-end=&quot;4927&quot;&gt;CalAIM Community Supports (preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4930&quot; data-end=&quot;5068&quot;&gt;Comfortable working with individuals experiencing homelessness, serious mental illness, substance use disorders, and complex social needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5071&quot; data-end=&quot;5154&quot;&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented; able to manage multiple cases simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5157&quot; data-end=&quot;5213&quot;&gt;Confident communicator with strong documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5216&quot; data-end=&quot;5305&quot;&gt;Comfortable working across multiple systems (EHRs, HMIS, referral portals, spreadsheets).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5308&quot; data-end=&quot;5390&quot;&gt;Able to work independently in the field while remaining accountable to team goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5393&quot; data-end=&quot;5466&quot;&gt;Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation (field work required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;5468&quot; data-end=&quot;5496&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;5468&quot; data-end=&quot;5496&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5499&quot; data-end=&quot;5562&quot;&gt;Bilingual (Spanish strongly preferred; other languages a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5565&quot; data-end=&quot;5642&quot;&gt;Experience working in Los Angeles County and/or Kern County homeless systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5645&quot; data-end=&quot;5719&quot;&gt;Familiarity with Housing Deposit and Tenancy Sustaining billing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;5721&quot; data-end=&quot;5724&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;5726&quot; data-end=&quot;5737&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5741&quot; data-end=&quot;5778&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5781&quot; data-end=&quot;5795&quot;&gt;Paid sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5798&quot; data-end=&quot;5825&quot;&gt;Accrued paid time off (PTO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5828&quot; data-end=&quot;5868&quot;&gt;Hybrid work environment (field + remote)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5871&quot; data-end=&quot;5950&quot;&gt;Opportunities for growth within a rapidly scaling healthcare technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5953&quot; data-end=&quot;6025&quot;&gt;Meaningful work directly impacting housing stability and health outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;6027&quot; data-end=&quot;6030&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;6032&quot; data-end=&quot;6070&quot;&gt;Work Environment &amp;amp; Physical Demands&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;6072&quot; data-end=&quot;6369&quot;&gt;This role involves a combination of &lt;strong data-start=&quot;6108&quot; data-end=&quot;6128&quot;&gt;field-based work&lt;/strong&gt; (community visits, housing sites, member meetings) and &lt;strong data-start=&quot;6184&quot; data-end=&quot;6214&quot;&gt;remote administrative work&lt;/strong&gt;. Requires prolonged computer use, frequent phone calls, travel within service areas, and occasional lifting of light materials related to move-in support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Hourly pay range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$22&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$28 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Akido Labs, Inc. is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage qualified applicants of every background, ability, and life experience to contact us about appropriate employment opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Akido builds AI-powered doctors&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Akido is the first AI-native care provider, combining cutting-edge technology with a nationwide medical network to address America’s physician shortage and make exceptional healthcare universal. Its AI empowers doctors to deliver faster, more accurate, and more compassionate care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving 500K+ patients across California, Rhode Island, and New York, Akido offers primary and specialty care in 26 specialties—from serving&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fastcompany.com/91231274/how-one-la-doctor-is-using-ai-to-help-homeless-communities-get-medical-care&quot;&gt;unhoused communities&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;in Los Angeles to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-ai-doctor-will-see-new-york-ride-share-drivers-now-5ba53e6c?mod=Searchresults_pos1&amp;amp;page=1&quot;&gt;ride-share drivers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;in New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2015 (YC W15), Akido is expanding its risk-bearing care models and scaling&amp;nbsp;ScopeAI, its breakthrough clinical AI platform. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250515102298/en/Akido-Raises-%2460-Million-Series-B-to-Expand-Reach-of-ScopeAI-its-Breakthrough-Health-Artificial-Intelligence&quot;&gt;Read more about Akido’s $60M Series B&lt;/a&gt;. More info at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Akidolabs.com&quot;&gt;Akidolabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;RIPC Medical Group is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Primary Care Nurse Practitioner (NP)&lt;/strong&gt; to join a growing, clinician-led medical group delivering high-quality, value-based care in a fully outpatient setting. &amp;nbsp;This role offers the opportunity to care for a diverse patient population across the full spectrum of primary care services. You will work alongside a collaborative team with strong clinical and operational support, allowing you to focus on patient care while leveraging modern care models and technology. This is an exciting opportunity to be part of a mission-driven organization shaping the future of community-based primary care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide comprehensive primary care to patients across the full lifespan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See 16–20 patients per day in a 100% outpatient setting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver high-quality, patient-centered care aligned with value-based care principles&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with physicians, advanced practice providers, and care teams to coordinate care and improve outcomes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Practice in collaboration with physicians in accordance with Rhode Island regulations, including consultation and referral as appropriate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage an assigned patient panel, including preventive care and chronic disease management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in care coordination and quality improvement initiatives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Utilize EMR to document care and manage patient records&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform in-office procedures based on experience and scope of practice (optional)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide after-hours call coverage for your patient panel (shared model may be available)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engage in team-based care and contribute to a supportive, collaborative practice environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1kpdi1v&quot; data-start=&quot;399&quot; data-end=&quot;418&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;403&quot; data-end=&quot;418&quot;&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;420&quot; data-end=&quot;1320&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Graduate of an accredited Nurse Practitioner program (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Board certified as a Nurse Practitioner (FNP, AGNP, or related primary care specialty) (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Licensed or eligible for licensure as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) in Rhode Island&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Active DEA registration or eligibility to obtain (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Rhode Island Controlled Substances Registration (CSR) or eligibility to obtain (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Commitment to delivering patient-centered, value-based primary care (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Strong clinical judgment with ability to manage a broad range of primary care conditions&lt;br&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Comfortable working in a team-based, technology-enabled care environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Interest in quality improvement and population health initiatives (preferred)
